                <pb facs="0215" n="119" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg119"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Conger to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Pekin, China</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-04-19"><hi rendition="#italic">April 19,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 362.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith
                    translation of an Imperial decree published on the 17 th instant concerning
                    train bands and local volunteers.</p>
                <p>These organizations have existed from time immemorial, and this decree is
                    evidently intended to give them to understand that in the sweeping decrees
                    against the “Boxers” they are not included, yet ordering them not to make
                    trouble, etc.</p>
                <p>This whole matter of the “Boxers” seems to be a very difficult one for the
                    Government. Evidently, recognizing its weakness, it is trying to effect their
                    suppression without alienating or angering more of its subjects than is
                    absolutely necessary.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. H. Conger.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d102-a1.xml" xpointer="d102-a1"/>
            </div>
